 "final_message": "The mortgage application (BHL-26001) is submitted, and Sam and Nadia's intent to proceed is recorded with Brightpath.\n\n- **Application:** I filled it in from their profile and the pay and account figures, and submitted it once. I uploaded only the permitted documents. Those were the last 2 statements for each of the four personal accounts and the last 2 payslips for each of them. Nothing from the business account was shared. I also gave the credit-check and e-sign consents.\n- **Underwriting condition:** The underwriter asked about an $8,000 mobile deposit on 09/03 into Sam's checking. Sam and Nadia said it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan. I sent that explanation to Brightpath as a written response.\n- **Loan Estimate:** The rate is 6.25% (limit 6.5%), the monthly payment is $3,042.41 (limit $3,100), and closing costs are $12,850 (limit $14,000). Estimated cash to close is $122,850. All three are within their limits, so I signed the intent to proceed with both of their names.\n\nI haven't checked whether Brightpath has responded to the condition explanation.",
